answers.answer_text:
a) Suitable CSS rules:

body {
  background-color: gray;
}

h1 {
  text-align: center;
}

p {
  text-align: justify;
}

Explanation:
• background-color: gray gives the webpage a gray background.
• text-align: center centers the heading.
• text-align: justify makes paragraph text aligned evenly along both left and right margins.

b) An external stylesheet is more efficient for multi-page websites because the same CSS file can be linked to multiple HTML pages. Changes made to the external stylesheet automatically affect all linked pages. It reduces code duplication, improves consistency, makes maintenance easier and can improve loading performance because the stylesheet can be cached by the browser. Therefore, external CSS is preferable for large multi-page websites.

